[SUMMARY]
  [1] Sigma_{n>=1}|<n|S_W|G>|^2 = Var + <S_W>^2 - p0 E0^2  [T]  (E0=0 for Wilson => Var+<S_W>^2)
      d07 (2.1) 'Sigma = Var' holds iff <Omega|S_W|G> = <S_W>, i.e. ONLY on the diagonal Omega=G.
  [2] int sqrt(Var) <= sqrt(T int Var)  [T]  -- d07's '>=' is a sign error (h06 right).
      BUT the premise 'int A >= c sqrt(V)' is nevertheless TRUE (pointwise: A >= 6V(1-u_p)) --
      so withdrawing 'proposition 3.1' and 'Delta_max >= 0.276 L^2' is an OVER-retraction:
      the implication is valid, 0.276 L^2 is true (weak); the correct constant is O(L^4).
  [3] true numerator O(V) => delta_{S_W} >= c L^4 (c = 2.01 L1-route, 2.82 L2-route).
